TITLE:: Command
SUMMARY:: Base representation of a command with named parameters and an execution action.
CATEGORIES:: Control
RELATED:: Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/DeleteCommand, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/LegatoCommand, Classes/MidinoteCommand, Classes/Parameter, Classes/PartCommand, Classes/RightCommand, Classes/SetCommand, Classes/SnapCommand, Classes/TransposeCommand, Classes/UndoHistory, Classes/WriteCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Command:: represents an executable command. It defines a name, a list of accepted LINK::Classes/Parameter:: instances, and an optional execution action LINK::Classes/Function::. Ad-hoc instances pass an action to LINK::#*new::. Subclasses such as LINK::Classes/AmpCommand::, LINK::Classes/DeleteCommand::, LINK::Classes/LeftCommand::, LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand::, LINK::Classes/MidinoteCommand::, LINK::Classes/PartCommand::, LINK::Classes/RightCommand::, LINK::Classes/SetCommand::, LINK::Classes/SnapCommand::, LINK::Classes/TransposeCommand::, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand:: override LINK::#-execute:: instead of passing an action.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::Command::.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/String:: or LINK::Classes/Symbol:: naming the command.

ARGUMENT:: parameters
An optional LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Parameter:: instances that this command accepts (defaults to empty).

ARGUMENT:: action
An optional LINK::Classes/Function:: called on execution, receiving an arguments LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::Command:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: action
Returns the execution function for this command, if specified.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Function:: or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: afterImage
Returns the values written by the last LINK::#-execute::, for redo. The default is CODE::nil::. An editor calls this only after LINK::#-beforeImage:: returned a non-empty dictionary, and passes that dictionary as well.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary passed to LINK::#-execute::.

ARGUMENT:: before
The dictionary returned by LINK::#-beforeImage::. A command that can rebuild the after-image from CODE::args:: alone may ignore it.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: beforeImage
Reads the values LINK::#-execute:: is about to overwrite. The default is CODE::nil::, and the editor then records no undo step. A command that can reverse itself returns an LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from each changed note or drum step to those previous values, including CODE::nil:: when a key was absent.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary about to be passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: execute
Executes the command with the provided arguments dictionary.

ARGUMENT:: argsDict
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: mapping parameter names to parsed argument values.

RETURNS::
The result of the action function, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: getParameter
Retrieves a parameter definition by name.

ARGUMENT:: paramName
A LINK::Classes/String:: or LINK::Classes/Symbol:: matching the parameter name.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Parameter:: instance, or CODE::nil:: if not found.

METHOD:: isValid
Returns whether all defined parameters have valid argument values in the given dictionary.

ARGUMENT:: argsDict
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: containing argument values.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: name
The name of the command.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/String::.

METHOD:: parameterIsOffered
Returns whether the prompt should offer this parameter given the arguments committed so far. The default is CODE::true::. LINK::Classes/SetCommand:: hides CODE::values:: until CODE::key:: is present.

ARGUMENT:: param
The LINK::Classes/Parameter:: being considered.

ARGUMENT:: argsDict
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: of arguments committed so far, or CODE::nil::.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: parameters
The list of parameter definitions accepted by this command.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Parameter:: instances.

METHOD:: resolveParameter
Returns the parameter that should parse an argument. The default is CODE::param::. LINK::Classes/SetCommand:: returns the dispatched command's CODE::values:: parameter when the committed key names that command.

ARGUMENT:: param
The LINK::Classes/Parameter:: from this command's own list.

ARGUMENT:: argsDict
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: of arguments committed so far, or CODE::nil::.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Parameter::.

METHOD:: restore
Writes an image captured by LINK::#-beforeImage:: or LINK::#-afterImage:: back onto the notes. The default does nothing.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: undoCommand
The command whose before-image and after-image should be stored for this execution. The default is this command. LINK::Classes/SetCommand:: returns the dispatched command, so CODE::set key amp::, CODE::set key legato::, CODE::set key part::, and CODE::set key midinote:: record that command's step. An unknown key records a LINK::Classes/SetCommand:: step for the event key.

ARGUMENT:: args
The arguments dictionary about to be passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Command::.

PRIVATE:: init
